body:
/kind feature

**Description**

Today, IG router logs the lines like  these:
```
{"level":"info","ts":1676824105.6426558,"logger":"InferenceGraphRouter","msg":"Entering callService","url":"http://model-sim-predictor-default.kserve-test.svc.cluster.local/v1/models/model-sim:predict"}
{"level":"info","ts":1676824106.571642,"logger":"InferenceGraphRouter","msg":"elapsed time","step":"http://model-sim-predictor-default.kserve-test.svc.cluster.local/v1/models/model-sim:predict","time":0.929007853}
{"level":"info","ts":1676824106.571681,"logger":"InferenceGraphRouter","msg":"Entering callService","url":"http://qbo-us-predictor-default.kserve-test.svc.cluster.local/v1/models/qbo-us:predict"}
{"level":"info","ts":1676824106.5812716,"logger":"InferenceGraphRouter","msg":"elapsed time","step":"http://qbo-us-predictor-default.kserve-test.svc.cluster.local/v1/models/qbo-us:predict","time":0.009586548}
{"level":"info","ts":1676824106.581336,"logger":"InferenceGraphRouter","msg":"elapsed time","node":"root","time":0.938705362}
```
The router's [logger](https://github.com/kserve/kserve/blob/master/cmd/router/main.go#L205) is not configurable. Being an orchestrator and caller of so many nodes(ISVCs in IG), router's logs should have trace id in it that can help trace the request flow end-to-end.
This will let users see the whole trace of how a request went through end-to-end.

Every company has their own tracing headers that they use and putting these tracing headers as part of log lines (via log formatter) is super helpful in tracing the flow.

**Describe the solution you'd like**

We should let the user influence the router's logging config via `router` section of `inferenceservice-config` configmap. 

**Expected logs**
```
{"level":"info","mycompany-trace-id":"tracker-7e073c4f-2144-47ce-172881be0954","ts":1676824105.6426558,"logger":"InferenceGraphRouter","msg":"Entering callService","url":"http://model-sim-predictor-default.kserve-test.svc.cluster.local/v1/models/model-sim:predict"}
{"level":"info","mycompany-trace-id":"tracker-7e073c4f-2144-47ce-172881be0954","ts":1676824106.571642,"logger":"InferenceGraphRouter","msg":"elapsed time","step":"http://model-sim-predictor-default.kserve-test.svc.cluster.local/v1/models/model-sim:predict","time":0.929007853}
{"level":"info","mycompany-trace-id":"tracker-7e073c4f-2144-47ce-172881be0954","ts":1676824106.571681,"logger":"InferenceGraphRouter","msg":"Entering callService","url":"http://qbo-us-predictor-default.kserve-test.svc.cluster.local/v1/models/qbo-us:predict"}
{"level":"info","mycompany-trace-id":"tracker-7e073c4f-2144-47ce-172881be0954","ts":1676824106.5812716,"logger":"InferenceGraphRouter","msg":"elapsed time","step":"http://qbo-us-predictor-default.kserve-test.svc.cluster.local/v1/models/qbo-us:predict","time":0.009586548}
{"level":"info","mycompany-trace-id":"tracker-7e073c4f-2144-47ce-172881be0954","ts":1676824106.581336,"logger":"InferenceGraphRouter","msg":"elapsed time","node":"root","time":0.938705362}
```

See how every log line now has `"mycompany-trace-id":"tracker-7e073c4f-2144-47ce-172881be0954"`

/kind feature

**Describe the solution you'd like**
Currently for example `sklearn` model, user has to explicitly specify the serving runtime name to choose the runtime that can support v2 protocol because `kserve-sklearnserver` is marked for auto selection.

**Anything else you would like to add:**
One option is to add `protocolVersion` to the `SupportedModelFormat`

```
// +k8s:openapi-gen=true
type SupportedModelFormat struct {
	// Name of the model format.
	// +required
	Name string `json:"name"`
	// Version of the model format.
	// Used in validating that a predictor is supported by a runtime.
	// Can be "major", "major.minor" or "major.minor.patch".
	// +optional
	Version *string `json:"version,omitempty"`
        // Supported protocol version
        // v1
        // grpc-v1
        // grpc-v2
        // v2
        ProtocolVersion string `json:"protocolVersion,omitempty"`
	// Set to true to allow the ServingRuntime to be used for automatic model placement if
	// this model format is specified with no explicit runtime.
	// +optional
	AutoSelect *bool `json:"autoSelect,omitempty"`
}
```

/kind feature

**Describe the solution you'd like**
Currently, all the predictors implement the `ComponentImplementation` interface which defines a `Default` method. Each of the predictors reference the struct value of `Resources`. In all cases, [setResourceRequirementDefaults](https://github.com/kserve/kserve/blob/master/pkg/apis/serving/v1beta1/inference_service_defaults.go#L41) will get a nil value since `Resources` is not exposed on the struct. It would be extremely beneficial to be able to set a custom set of resource requirements in the spec such that it gets passed through to the inferenceservice. For example,


Exposing `Resources` (SKLearn in this example)
```
// SKLearnSpec defines arguments for configuring SKLearn model serving.
type SKLearnSpec struct {
	// Contains fields shared across all predictors
	PredictorExtensionSpec `json:",inline"`
	// Resources
	Resources v1.ResourceRequirements
}
```
```
func (k *SKLearnSpec) Default(config *InferenceServicesConfig) {
	k.Container.Name = constants.InferenceServiceContainerName

	if k.RuntimeVersion == nil {
		defaultVersion := config.Predictors.SKlearn.V1.DefaultImageVersion
		if k.ProtocolVersion != nil && *k.ProtocolVersion == constants.ProtocolV2 {
			defaultVersion = config.Predictors.SKlearn.V2.DefaultImageVersion
		}

		k.RuntimeVersion = &defaultVersion
	}

	if k.ProtocolVersion == nil {
		defaultProtocol := constants.ProtocolV1
		k.ProtocolVersion = &defaultProtocol
	}

	setResourceRequirementDefaults(&k.Resources)
}
```



```
	v1beta.InferenceServiceSpec{
		Predictor: v1beta.PredictorSpec{
			SKLearn: &v1beta.SKLearnSpec{
				PredictorExtensionSpec: v1beta.PredictorExtensionSpec{},
				Resources: v1.ResourceRequirements{
					Requests: v1.ResourceList{
						v1.ResourceCPU:    resource.MustParse("MY CUSTOM CPU REQUEST HERE"),
						v1.ResourceMemory: resource.MustParse("MY CUSTOM MEMORY REQUEST HERE"),
					},
					Limits: v1.ResourceList{
						v1.ResourceCPU:    resource.MustParse("MY CUSTOM CPU LIMIT HERE"),
						v1.ResourceMemory: resource.MustParse("MY CUSTOM MEMORY LIMIT HERE"),
					},
				},
			},
		},
	}

``` 

If it makes more sense, Resources could also sit in the `PredictorExtensionSpec`. Perhaps adding annotation support such as done for [autoscaling](https://github.com/kserve/kserve/blob/master/pkg/controller/v1beta1/inferenceservice/reconcilers/knative/ksvc_reconciler.go#L64-L82) would be beneficial as well.



**Anything else you would like to add:**
I know there is an [issue](https://github.com/kserve/kserve/issues/1593) out to fix the defaults globally but this falls outside of that scope (I think)
